# ARK Square Payments

Square is a **capture rail**, not financial authority.

All money truth flows through existing financial core:

- `BalanceDueCalculator` — amount authority
- `RecordLedgerEntryAction` — ledger writes
- `RepairOrderPaymentPostureSync` — RO payment posture (temporary compat layer)
- Invoice snapshots — historical invoice total truth

Square never calculates totals, never posts ledger entries directly from the browser, and never becomes a competing balance source.

## Capture Surfaces (In Scope)

| Surface | Who | How | Primary UX |
|---------|-----|-----|------------|
| **Counter — Terminal** | Staff | Square Terminal API + paired reader | "Charge card" on financial rail; reader prompts customer |
| **Counter — Keyed** | Staff | Square Web Payments SDK | Fallback when reader unavailable; card entry in ARK modal |
| **Portal** | Customer | Web Payments SDK on `/portal/*` | Pay balance on issued invoice from customer portal |
| **Emailed invoice** | Customer | Signed pay link in invoice email | "Pay now" CTA → hosted pay page (same SDK, tokenized session) |

Manual **Record Payment** (cash, check, external swipe) remains forever as fallback. Do not remove.

## Convergence Architecture

One gateway pipeline, four entry points:

```
Entry surface (staff terminal / staff keyed / portal / email link)
        ↓
InitiateSquarePaymentAction
  - amount from BalanceDueCalculator (server)
  - links repair_order_id + financial_document_id (issued invoice)
  - creates gateway_attempt (pending) + idempotency_key
        ↓
Square API (Terminal checkout OR Payments API with source_id from Web SDK)
        ↓
Webhook payment.updated (queued) OR staff poll for Terminal in-flight
        ↓
CompleteSquarePaymentAction
  - verify amount, status, idempotency
  - RecordLedgerEntryAction::recordPayment()
  - store square_payment_id on attempt + ledger reference
        ↓
RepairOrderPaymentPostureSync + OperationalEvent (RepairOrderPaymentReceived)
```

### Frozen rules

- Ledger entry only after Square status is **COMPLETED** (or equivalent terminal success).
- Never record optimistic payments.
- Partial payments allowed — charge amount ≤ balance due unless overpayment/store-credit path already handles excess.
- Refunds go through Square Refunds API, then `recordRefund()` on ledger.
- Deposits via Square are a separate initiate path using `recordDeposit()` — same gateway, different ledger type.
- PCI: ARK never stores or transmits raw card numbers. Terminal and Web Payments SDK tokenize.

## Schema (Gateway Layer)

Add gateway tracking separate from ledger truth:

**`payment_gateway_attempts`** (or equivalent)

- `repair_order_id`, `customer_id`, `financial_document_id`
- `gateway` = `square`
- `capture_surface` = `terminal` | `keyed` | `portal` | `email`
- `amount_cents`, `currency`
- `idempotency_key` (unique)
- `square_payment_id`, `square_checkout_id`, `square_device_id` (nullable per surface)
- `status` = `pending` | `completed` | `failed` | `canceled` | `refunded`
- `failure_reason`, `processing_fee_cents` (nullable, from Square when available)
- `initiated_by` (staff user, nullable for customer surfaces)
- `customer_access_token_id` (nullable — portal/email sessions)
- `ledger_entry_id` (nullable until completed)
- timestamps: `initiated_at`, `completed_at`

Ledger `reference` should include Square payment ID for reconciliation even when gateway row exists.

## Shop Configuration

Encrypted shop settings (or dedicated `square_connections` table):

- Application ID (public — needed for Web SDK)
- Access token / OAuth refresh (encrypted)
- Location ID
- Environment: sandbox | production
- Terminal device registry (device_id, label, paired_at)
- Webhook signature key
- Feature toggles per surface (terminal on, keyed on, portal pay on, email pay on)

Terminal pairing requires **Connected / Terminal API mode** on the physical reader — not Square Register/POS mode. Settings → Payments → **Generate pairing code** calls Square `CreateDeviceCode` (`TERMINAL_API`, production only); staff sign out on reader, tap **Device Code**, enter code within 5 minutes. Paired `device_id` auto-saves via `device.code.paired` webhook or status poll. Manual paste still supported. [Square pairing guide](https://developer.squareup.com/docs/terminal-api/integrate-square-terminal). ARKademy `square-payments-setup` is staff authority.

## Surface-Specific Behavior

### Counter — Terminal

- Visible on financial rail when `canRecordPayment` and Square terminal enabled.
- Default amount = current balance due; staff may lower for partial.
- Initiate → Terminal checkout → poll or push status until complete/timeout.
- Show "Waiting on reader" state; allow cancel in-flight checkout.
- AJAX continuity on financial rail refresh after completion.

### Counter — Keyed

- Secondary action: "Enter card" when terminal unavailable or customer requests keyed.
- Load Square Web Payments SDK; tokenize to `source_id`.
- Server charges via Payments API — same `CompleteSquarePaymentAction` path.
- Never expose secret keys to frontend; only Application ID + location.

### Portal

- Requires customer portal auth or signed document access (see Customer Access).
- Portal invoice view shows balance due from server snapshot + live balance check.
- "Pay with card" when invoice issued and balance > 0.
- Calm, mobile-first, trust-oriented layout per portal surface rules.
- Payment success → portal confirmation + staff notification event.

### Emailed invoice

- Extend invoice email delivery (not estimate-only) with optional pay link.
- Email contains signed, time-limited pay URL — not a permanent portal login.
- Pay page reuses same Web Payments flow as portal (shared pay component).
- Log `OperationalCommunicationType::InvoiceSent` (or equivalent) with pay-link flag.
- PDF attachment remains; pay link is additive CTA.

## Customer Access (Portal + Email)

Portal is currently a stub. Payment epic requires a minimal access boundary:

**Option A — signed pay tokens (MVP for email)**

- `customer_document_access_tokens`: repair_order_id, document_id, token hash, expires_at, scope=`pay_invoice`
- Email link: `/portal/pay/{token}`
- No full portal account required for email pay

**Option B — portal session (for logged-in portal)**

- Customer guard + vehicle/RO association
- Reuse same pay controller with session auth instead of token

Build token path first for emailed invoices; portal auth can layer on later without forking payment logic.

## Staff UI Placement

Primary: `financial-rail.blade.php` on RO workspace (Ready for Pickup + issued invoice).

- "Charge with Square" (terminal primary)
- "Enter card" (keyed secondary)
- Existing manual Record Payment form unchanged below

Settings: shop settings area — Square connection, terminal pairing, surface toggles, sandbox switch.

## Webhooks & Reliability

- `POST /webhooks/square` — signature verified, queued handler
- Idempotent completion: if `ledger_entry_id` already set, acknowledge and exit
- Failed webhooks retry-safe
- Horizon queue for webhook processing
- Operational event on failure for staff visibility

## Testing Strategy

- Mock Square API in feature tests; no live network in CI
- Assert: no ledger entry on pending/failed
- Assert: single ledger entry on duplicate webhook
- Assert: amount always from server balance, not request tampering
- Sandbox manual QA: Terminal device, keyed modal, email link, portal page
- MySQL only — gateway tables follow ARK database rules

## Epic Phases

### Phase 1 — Gateway foundation

- Schema: `payment_gateway_attempts`, shop Square config
- `SquareClient` wrapper (official `square/square` SDK justified)
- `InitiateSquarePaymentAction`, `CompleteSquarePaymentAction`
- Webhook controller + queued handler
- Feature tests with mocked Square

### Phase 2 — Counter capture

- Terminal initiate + status polling on financial rail
- Keyed Web Payments modal on financial rail
- Settings: credentials, location, device pairing
- Manual QA with Square sandbox

### Phase 3 — Customer pay (email + portal)

- Customer access tokens for signed pay links
- Shared portal pay page + Web Payments SDK
- Invoice email with pay CTA (issued invoice only, balance > 0)
- Portal stub → minimal invoice/pay view (read-first, calm)

### Phase 4 — Money lifecycle completion

- Square refunds → ledger refund entries
- Deposits via Square at drop-off (optional if shop needs)
- Reconciliation helper: Square payment ID ↔ ledger entries
- Processing fee capture for overhead accuracy (optional)

## Out of Scope (Unless Explicitly Authorized)

- Multi-processor abstraction (Stripe, etc.) — build Square direct first
- Financing / BNPL
- Recurring billing / stored cards on file
- Customer tipping
- Replacing Square standalone POS
- Financial logic changes to `EstimateTotalsCalculator` or invoice snapshots

## Dependency Justification

`square/square` PHP SDK solves OAuth, Terminal API, Payments API, Refunds, and webhook payload typing. Symfony HttpClient alone is insufficient for operational reliability at this integration depth.

## Success Test

Advisor or customer pays an issued invoice balance. ARK ledger, balance due, payment posture, and closeout gating update exactly as they do today for manual card entry — but the Square payment ID is traceable and the advisor did not re-type the amount after a successful charge.
